return {
["18:00"]={"King Richard: What is o’clock?\nCatesby: It is \003six o’clock\004, full supper time.\nKing Richard: I will not sup tonight. Give me some ink and paper.","Richard III","William Shakespeare"},
["18:01"]={"“No one stops, even to draw breath, until \003one minute past six\004 when the last vote will have been cast.”","Sons of Fortune","Jeffrey Archer"},
["18:02"]={"Incidentally, confirmed by a record of a small and poorly defined shallow-focus earthquake around two hundred and fifty kilometers north of Herrandown at \0036:02 p.m.\004 But there is a major problem.","The Shadow and Night","Chris Walley"},
["18:03"]={"Jarrod stared at the clock on his computer. It said \0036:03\004. Outside his office window it was dark. It felt as if someone had sucked all the oxygen from the room and he took an extra breath before responding.","All the Little Pieces","Jilliane Hoffman"},
["18:04"]={"We will make record of it, my Rosannah; every year, as this dear hour chimes from the clock, we will celebrate it with thanksgivings, all the years of our life.\n“We will, we will, Alonzo!”\n“\003Four minutes after six\004, in the evening, my Rosannah…”","The Loves of Alonzo Fitz Clarence and Rosannah Ethelton","Mark Twain"},
["18:05"]={"\0036:05 p.m.\004 Wonder where everybody is? I suppose they are all out with their boyfriends or have gone home to their families.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["18:06"]={"According to the Book of Revelation, the great beast’s number is 666. So that exact time would be \003six minutes past six\004 on the sixth of the sixth, sixty-six. Double whammy.","A Dog Called Demolition","Robert Rankin"},
["18:07"]={"The minutes ticked by. The silence in the room roared in their ears. At \003seven minutes past six\004, Charles’s phone rang.","The Jury","Fern Michaels"},
["18:08"]={"\0036:08 p.m.\004 The code-word “Valkyrie” reached von Seydlitz Gabler’s headquarters","The Night of the Generals","Hans Hellmut Kirst"},
["18:09"]={"Here I am, at \003nine minutes past six\004 on a drizzly Saturday evening, with every intention of writing a book in one sitting.","Life With No Breaks","Nick Spalding"},
["18:10"]={"‘I’d like to see your passenger list for yesterday afternoon’s \0036:10\004 flight for Brussels.’","Over My Dead Body","Jeffrey Archer"},
["18:11"]={"The first explosion occurred at \003eleven minutes past six\004. The chart-house and part of the bridge were blown to pieces. Three dull, splintering crashes ensued in rapid succession, proving beyond question that the bombs were set to automatically explode at a given time.","West Wind Drift","George Barr McCutcheon"},
["18:12"]={"At \00306:12\004 Noreen brings another whole tray that’s dinner, we can have dinner at five something or six something or even seven something, Ma says.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["18:13"]={"It’s \00306:13\004, that’s getting nearly to be the evening. Ma says I really should be wrapped up in Rug already, Old Nick might possibly come in early because of me being sick.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["18:15"]={"I checked the time on the corner of my screen. \0036:15 pm.\004 I was never going to finish my essay in forty-five minutes","Girl Missing","Sophie McKenzie"},
["18:16"]={"The clock above the door said \003sixteen minutes past six\004. The pictures showed the door opening and a rug coming in — just the rug, flat, held up perpendicular, hanging straight down. Of course there was someone behind it.","If Death Ever Slept","Rex Stout"},
["18:17"]={"The printed front of the card read Bernis Sand. On the back was written in pencil: your westbound tram stop at \00318:17\004. There was no date or signature. At 18:17 Adele stepped out of the townhouse with Trovera at her side.","The Way to Glory","David Drake"},
["18:18"]={"It was at \00318:18\004 when a sixty-one-year-old Tibetan woman telephoned for a fire engine to put out a burning car.","My Name is Not Jacob Ramsay","Ben Trebilcook"},
["18:19"]={"Gravesend’s a black cloud. Vinny and Stella and Mam are in it. Are it. My watch says \00318:19\004 and the Captain Marlow’ll be cheerful and chattery as the evening regulars drift in.","The Bone Clocks","David Mitchell"},
["18:20"]={"By the time Elliot’s mother arrived at \003twenty past six\004, Mrs. Sen always made sure all evidence of her chopping was disposed of.","Interpreter of Maladies","Jhumpa Lahiri"},
["18:22"]={"It was \003six twenty-two\004, Commander. I happened to glance at the clock.\nHe held open the door wide. It seemed less an invitation to leave than a command.","The Murder Room","P.D. James"},
["18:23"]={"A picnic lunch in the kitchen, a double bolt drawn across the front door just in case the impossible happened and Father came home from the bank before \003twenty-three minutes past six\004 in the evening.","Light a Penny Candle","Maeve Binchy"},
["18:24"]={"We were cleared by the tower at \00318:24\004 and got airborne seven minutes after the scheduled departure time. The evening sky was almost clear, with a scattering of cumulous along the southern horizon and the windsocks hanging limp.","Quiller’s Run","Adam Hall"},
["18:25"]={"I have this moment, while writing, had a wire from Jonathan saying that he leaves by the \0036:25\004 tonight from Launceston and will be here at 10:18, so that I shall have no fear tonight.","Dracula","Bram Stoker"},
["18:26"]={"I checked the time on my mobile phone — \00318:26 p.m.\004\n“Do you want to grab a pizza?” Cara asked as she walked in twenty minutes later. I looked up at her. She shook her head smiling, questioning.","Play With Me","Ananth"},
["18:27"]={"It was \0036:27\004. In Frances Peverell’s flat the phone rang. As soon as James spoke her name she knew that something was wrong.","Original Sin","P.D. James"},
["18:28"]={"At \0036:28 p.m.\004, a “Breaking News Alert” from the Examiner flashed to mobile phones and computers throughout the Chicago area: “Thomas R. O’Sullivan III, youngest member of once-powerful Illinois political family, among two slain in Diamond Point holdup. Lone gunman sought.”","The Ambition","Lee Strobel"},
["18:29"]={"Lieutenant Hershel Mote could not keep the note of near hysteria out of his voice when Wesley returned his telephone call at \003twenty-nine minutes past six p.m.\004\n“You’re where?” Wesley asked him again on the speaker phone.","The Body Farm","Patricia Cornwell"},
["18:30"]={"It is \003six thirty\004. Now the dark night and the deafening racket of the crickets again engulf the garden and the veranda, all around the house","Jealousy","Alain Robbe-Grillet"},
["18:31"]={"“The actions,” Captain Berry relates, “commenced at sunset, which was at \003thirty-one minutes past six, p.m.\004, with an ardour and vigour which it is impossible to describe.”","The Story of Nelson","Harold F.B. Wheeler"},
["18:32"]={"As he stepped out of the great Gothic cathedral it started to rain. Septimus reluctantly undid his neatly rolled umbrella and, putting it up, dashed through the puddles, hoping he would be in time to catch the \0036:32\004.","Broken Routine","Jeffrey Archer"},
["18:33"]={"Every evening, Michel took the train home, changed at Esbly and usually arrived in Crécy on the \0036:33 pm\004 train where Annabelle would be waiting at the station.","Atomised","Michel Houellebecq"},
["18:34"]={"It is \003around half past six\004 in the evening. Dusk is gathering in the living room, an early dusk due to the fog which has rolled in from the Sound and is like a white curtain drawn down outside the windows.","Long Day’s Journey Into Night","Eugene O’Neill"},
["18:35"]={"I swipe for the time with wet thumbs: \0036:35 p.m.\004 I’m early. Very early. I’d consider this a good thing if any part of my plan could be called that. I swallow. None of my plan is certain.","Bath Haus","P.J. Vernon"},
["18:36"]={"Kaldren pursues me like luminescent shadow. He has chalked up on the gateway ‘96,688,365,498,702’. Should confuse the mail man. Woke 9:05. To sleep \0036:36\004.","The Voices of Time","J.G. Ballard"},
["18:37"]={"Amy: What’s that? I thought I saw someone pass the window. What time is it?\nCharles: \003Nearly twenty to seven\004.","The Family Reunion","T.S. Eliot"},
["18:39"]={"At \003twenty-one minutes to seven\004, Yuri will sit down at your table, or maybe at the one next to it. That will obviously depend on how busy the cafe is.","Manhunt","James Barrington"},
["18:40"]={"Having to change ’buses, I allowed plenty of time — in fact, too much; for we arrived at \003twenty minutes to seven\004, and Franching, so the servant said, had only just gone up to dress.","The Diary of a Nobody","George and Weedon Grossmith"},
["18:41"]={"He made it to Grand Central well in advance. Stillman’s train was not due to arrive until \003six forty-one\004, but Quinn wanted time to study the geography of the place, to make sure that Stillman would not be able to slip away from him.","The New York Trilogy","Paul Auster"},
["18:42"]={"It was \003six forty-two\004. Unless Emma was spending the weekend out of town she would probably be at home.","A Taste for Death","P.D. James"},
["18:43"]={"Bev was no clock-watcher, but by \00318:43\004 she’d had enough. A stack of papers at her left elbow represented eliminations: calls put in, checks made, follow-ups done and dusted. At the right lay further actions.","Bad Press","Maureen Carter"},
["18:45"]={"\003Six forty-five\004, called Louie. “Did you hear, Ming,” he asked, “did you hear?”\n“Yes, Taddy, I heard.”\n“What is it?” asked Tommy. “The new baby, listen, the new baby.”","The Man Who Loved Children","Christina Stead"},
["18:46"]={"When I heard the thump overhead, I did not bother to look up. I knew it was \003fourteen minutes to seven\004.","Tiffany Street","Jerome Weidman"},
["18:47"]={"The clock said \0036:47 pm\004. With growing fear, I walked stiffly around the apartment, turning on all the lights — even the overhead lights in the living room, which we generally didn’t use because they were so stark and bright.","The Goldfinch","Donna Tartt"},
["18:48"]={"We were soon dashing quickly along the streets. I did not know Liverpool well, and consequently could not tell exactly where the man was going. When I got into the hansom it wanted \003twelve minutes to seven o’clock\004; these minutes were quickly flying, and still no station.","A Master of Mysteries","Robert Eustace"},
["18:49"]={"\0036:49 p.m.\004 Lieutenant-General Tanz escorted by a motorized unit, drove to Corps headquarters","The Night of the Generals","Hans Hellmut Kirst"},
["18:50"]={"It was time to go see the Lady. When we arrived at her house at \003ten minutes before seven\004 o’clock, Damaronde answered the door.","Boy’s Life","Robert R. McCammon"},
["18:51"]={"The square of light in the kitchen doorway had faded to thin purple; his watch said \0036:51\004.","Salem’s Lot","Stephen King"},
["18:52"]={"We’ve missed the train! It’s ten —\003eight— minutes to seven\004, said Arthur, in a voice which combined reproach and terror. And he sprang out of bed and began with hysteric fury to sort out his garments.","Catching the Train","Arnold Bennett"},
["18:53"]={"He strolled across the tarmac to the waiting plane \003a few minutes after six-fifty\004. The plane carrying the icon would be touching down in Washington in about two hours.","A Matter of Honor","Jeffrey Archer"},
["18:54"]={"I feel a little awkward, Kay Randall said on the phone, “asking a man to do these errands … but that’s my problem, not yours. Just bring the supplies and try to be at the church meeting room \003a few minutes before seven\004.”","Bridging","Max Apple"},
["18:55"]={"… You had no reason to think the times important. Indeed how suspicious it would be if you had been completely accurate.\n“Haven’t I been?”\n“Not quite. It was \003five to seven\004 that you talked to Wilkins.”\n“Another ten minutes.”","The Quiet American","Graham Greene"},
["18:56"]={"Then it was \0036:56\004. A black Rover — a Rover 90, registration PYX 520 — turned into the street that ran down the left-hand side of The Bunker. It parked. The door on the driver’s side opened. A man got out.","Dreams of Leaving","Rupert Thomson"},
["18:58"]={"Today was Tuesday, the fifteenth of August; the sun had risen at eleven minutes past five this morning and would set at \003two minutes before seven\004 this evening.","The Hot Rock","Donald E. Westlake"},
["18:59"]={"At \0036:59 p.m.\004 Central Standard Time, I stand in my Sunday best in Clare’s vestibule with my finger on her buzzer, fragrant yellow freesia and an Australian Cabernet in my other arm, and my heart in my mouth.","The Time Traveler’s Wife","Audrey Niffenegger"},
